Subject: [PATCH] build: Require a compatible scanner for enum headers

The SDK's wayland-scanner 1.23.1 rejects the frozen interface attribute
when generating enum headers with --strict. Use the same scanner
minimum as the protocol tests for this optional header generation.
The XML files and pkg-config metadata still install with an older
scanner, as they do when the optional scanner is unavailable.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@
 
 include_dirs = []
 headers = []
-if dep_scanner.found()
+if dep_scanner.found() and dep_scanner.version().version_compare('>=1.25.0')
 	subdir('include/wayland-protocols')
 	include_dirs = ['include']
 endif
